://scontent-lga3-3.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/499619187_2286222405545549_3933717362258917330_n.png?_nc_cat=106&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=wXPWnaaOISkQ7kNvwGXd7AP&_nc_oc=AdoT0qB_MbGMg0UBjBmA4cwi8ahuKn5hVbC4vJgANT_G9BlMVsgkRLlv2VNpA8S5Rgo&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-lga3-3.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQMVy-E8dUIZnnQYoTmOQXJuApT0e6BpEahnmCQMBL_-ww&oe=6AC4F34E"}, "display_name": "Mirror Android Phone Control", "keywords": ["phone"], "long_description": "Mirror Android Phone Control lets you view and control your Android phone directly inside Meta Quest.\n\nConnect your Android phone and Quest headset over the same Wi-Fi network, then access your phone screen without removing your headset.\n\nYou can interact with your phone using Quest controllers or hand tracking, making it easy to use Android apps while staying in VR or mixed reality.\n\nKey features include:\n\nMirror your Android phone screen in real time\nControl your phone from Meta Quest\nTap, swipe, scroll, and navigate Android apps\nUse Quest controllers or hand tracking for interaction\nEnter text using the Meta Quest system keyboard\nResize and position the phone screen anywhere in your VR or mixed reality space\nConnect over your local Wi-Fi network\nKeep using your Android phone without taking off your headset\n\nMirror Android Phone Control is useful for checking messages, controlling apps, viewing content, or accessing your Android device while working, playing, or relaxing in VR.\n\nA companion Android app may be required for phone mirroring and remote control features.\n\nSome features may require additional Android permissions depending on your device and Android version.", "short_description": "Mirror and control your Android phone directly from your Meta Quest headset."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "http://minsol.pe.kr/phone/PrivacyPolicy.html", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "woojoung", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "http